- op: discuss  # d789
  at: '2026-05-20T18:16:36Z'  # d789
  by: agent  # d789
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d789
  clock: 6  # d789
  nonce: d789  # d789
  message: "Fixed in PR merged 2026-05-20 (commit 9046ecf7cb). Root cause: get_language_extensions() and get_analyzable_extensions() in taxonomy.py injected LANGUAGE_ALIASES as duplicate keys, causing profile.py:_detect_languages to enumerate the same .sh files twice ('bash' + 'shell'). Fix: dropped the alias-injection loops in both functions; aliases now resolved at lookup time via LANGUAGE_ALIASES.get(name, name) by the sole alias-aware caller (partial_install_warnings.py). Cross-language audit per Structural Fix Protocol confirmed the bug is isolated to taxonomy.py — _CATALOG_ALIASES (io_boundary.py) and _FRAMEWORK_ALIASES (framework_patterns.py) both use the safe .get(id, id) pattern. New invariants: property tests assert set(LANGUAGE_EXTENSIONS).isdisjoint(LANGUAGE_ALIASES) AND set(SOURCE_EXTENSIONS).isdisjoint(LANGUAGE_ALIASES); end-to-end test_inv_tosum_bash_not_double_counted runs run_behavior_map on a 2-file .sh fixture and asserts languages['bash']['files']==2 AND 'shell' not in languages. Closes the first child of META INV-tolaj (Wave 4)."  # d789
